<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdullah of Pahang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1959">1959</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Al-Sultan Abdullah Ri'ayatuddin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdullah of Pahang, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Abdullah Ri'ayatuddin, became sultan of Pahang in January 2019 on the abdication of his father, Sultan Ahmad Shah. Later that month he was elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-di-pertuan-agong">Yang di-Pertuan Agong</a>, the king of Malaysia, and served a five-year term until January 2024, a period that included the political crises of 2020 to 2022.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abdullah-of-pahang.jpg" alt="Abdullah of Pahang" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 首相官邸ホームページ · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Abdullah_of_Pahang_(cropped_3to4_portrait).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
